   "Amphibians remain largely unmapped as interaction partners: Pristimantis spp., Epipedobates darwinwallacei, glassfrogs, and their predator/parasite links need dedicated extraction.",
   "Reptile interactions are still nearly absent except one predation note; priority taxa include Bothrocophias campbelli, Chironius spp., dipsadid snake guilds, and lizard–arthropod prey links from Mindo-Tandayapa.",
   "Large frugivorous birds that should be prioritized next include Semnornis ramphastinus, Chamaepetes goudotii, Rupicola peruvianus, and mixed-flock tanagers/cotingas.",
   "Non-bat mammals are still thinly represented; priority taxa include Bassaricyon neblina, Cebus capucinus, Tremarctos ornatus, Pecari tajacu, Microsciurus mimulus, and Didelphis spp.",
   "Euglossini–orchid interactions are still missing despite clear relevance to the corridor; this is one of the best next non-hummingbird layers to add.",
   "Ithomiini host-plant coverage is still too narrow; only Mechanitis menapis mantineus yielded a high-confidence edge from the accessible sources.",
   "Parasitism remains underdeveloped beyond avian malaria; Philornis host pairs, bat flies, ticks, mites, and helminths for corridor vertebrates should be prioritized.",
   "Epiphyte–host, ant–plant, galler–host, and mycorrhizal edges were not recovered with sufficient confidence from openly accessible material in this pass."
  ]
